<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shamsuddin Muhammad Shah Ghazi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1554">1554</a>–<a href="/years/1555">1555</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad Khan Sur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shamsuddin Muhammad Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a>, born Muhammad Khan Sur, was the governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sur-empire">Sur Empire</a> who declared independence after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam-shah-suri">Islam Shah Suri</a> in 1554. He founded a short-lived Afghan line of Bengal sultans. Marching west to claim power in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, he was defeated and killed at Chhapar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghat">Ghat</a> near Kalpi in 1555 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hemu">Hemu</a>, general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> Suri.</p></div>
